    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "You mentioned that critics are \"correct\" about the risk of capital flight. Doesn't that imply that the economic risk is a more certain, proven outcome compared to the theoretical benefits of reducing inequality? Like, we can see people moving money, so isn't it more accurate to say the danger is real while the benefits are just an idea?",
